## Scope

Green changed three production files and added one:

- `apps/storytime/lib/contracts/week.ts` (changed): the exports `shareShotSchema` and
  `shareSchema`, and the field `share: shareSchema.optional()` in `scriptSchema`.
- `apps/storytime/lib/share-moment.ts` (new): the consent line, the media labels, and the rule
  that finds the shot of a step.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/teacher/[level]/[week]/[day]/lesson-flow.tsx` (changed): the
  share moment in the step view.

No committed Red test changed. No week file, no received content, no read-along package, and no
Primary file changed.

## The contract that Green implemented

1. `lib/contracts/week.ts` exports `shareShotSchema` and `shareSchema`. The script schema holds
   `share: shareSchema.optional()`. The shot object holds `step` and `media`, and it is strict.
   The share object holds one or two shots and the caption, and it is strict. The caption uses
   the shared `biText`.
2. `lib/share-moment.ts` exports `SHARE_CONSENT_LINE` with `en` and `th` text. It also holds
   `SHARE_MEDIA_LABELS` and the rule `shareShotAt`.
3. `TeacherLessonFlow` shows the moment only when `loopsApproved(week)` is true. The rule reads
   the approval with the module `lib/loops`, so the client screen loads no week contract.
4. The moment shows only at a step of its own day. A shot that names a step of another day shows
   nowhere, and the app adds no fallback. The day 5 shot of the shipped week names D6, and day 5
   holds E1 to E5, so day 5 shows no moment.
5. The moment carries `data-share-moment`, `data-share-media`, and an element with
   `data-share-label`. It shows the caption and the consent line in the language of the flow.
6. The moment holds no control. The app sends no photo and no video.

The eight received week files hold the share field. All of them parse with the new contract.

